# Example torrc snippet: enable the control port with cookie authentication.
#
# This is a SAMPLE. Paths are placeholders — adjust to match your distro's Tor
# packaging (Debian/Ubuntu use the debian-tor user and /run/tor; other distros differ).
# Do NOT commit a real HashedControlPassword or a real cookie file.

# --- Control port -------------------------------------------------------------
# Listen for control connections on loopback only. Never expose the control port
# to the network — anyone who can reach it can drive your Tor client.
ControlPort 9051

# --- Authentication (choose ONE of the two below) -----------------------------

# Option A: cookie authentication (recommended for local automation).
# Tor writes a per-session cookie file; only processes that can read it can
# authenticate. tor-rotate.sh reads this cookie automatically.
CookieAuthentication 1
# Optional: make the cookie group-readable so a non-root automation user in the
# tor group can read it. Leave commented unless you actually need it.
# CookieAuthFileGroupReadable 1
# CookieAuthFile /run/tor/control.authcookie      # placeholder path — verify on your system

# Option B: password authentication (instead of the cookie above).
# Generate the hash with:  tor --hash-password 'YOUR-PASSWORD'
# Then paste the resulting 16:... hash below. The hash shown here is a
# PLACEHOLDER and authenticates nothing — replace it.
# HashedControlPassword 16:REPLACE_WITH_OUTPUT_OF_tor_hash_password

# --- SOCKS port ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Default SOCKS proxy your clients connect to. Bind to loopback only.
# Remember: resolve hostnames THROUGH this proxy (socks5h:// / --socks5-hostname
# / torsocks) — see docs/socks5-dns-leak.md.
SocksPort 9050

# --- Optional: circuit behavior ----------------------------------------------
# NewCircuitPeriod governs how often Tor considers building fresh circuits. The
# NEWNYM coalescing floor (~10s) is a compiled constant and is not set here; see
# docs/newnym-rate-limit.md.
# NewCircuitPeriod 30
